content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-105, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22000, on the filtered-water line. P-105 is within the P-101 to P-106 group whose water is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite (C16).",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the reported 3.9 mm/s is numerically within Figure 3 Zone B, 2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below Zone C at 4.5 mm/s RMS, where maintenance planning is required, and below Zone D at 7.1 mm/s RMS, where damage is likely and the pump must be stopped. The applicable method is vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings, classifying the highest reading from both housings. The report does not confirm RMS, measurement location, or the other housing reading, so this classification is conditional on confirmation of those details.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing temperature: 71 °C is 1 °C above the documented normal bearing-housing limit of up to 70 °C, but remains 9 °C below the 80 °C alarm and 19 °C below the 90 °C trip. These limits apply to temperature measured on the bearing-housing surface. Investigate grease quantity, bearing condition and alignment during the planned repair; the reading is above normal but is not an alarm or trip condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage: leakage at the shaft seal is a documented symptom requiring mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. No allowable leakage rate is supplied, so the active leak cannot be accepted by comparison with a numerical leak limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Priority/stop basis: plan a P2 repair for the active seal leak and above-normal housing temperature. Neither numeric reading reaches its documented immediate-stop criterion: the vibration is below the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone D threshold and the temperature is below the 90 °C trip. The pump must nevertheless be isolated and drained before the seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Leading asset-specific possibility, if the original component seal is still fitted: early failure of HF3-450 caused by the revised sleeve tolerance. The bulletin documents such field failures on pumps built from serial HF3-22000 onward, and P-105 is exactly serial HF3-22000. The installed seal type has not been reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces are a documented direct cause of leakage at the shaft seal; confirm during disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal may have run dry. No operating or flush history is supplied; the manual specifies Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and warns never to run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is another documented cause of shaft-seal leakage and can also be associated with high bearing temperature; alignment must therefore be checked.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing or bearing wear may explain the housing temperature being above normal, but 71 °C alone does not establish which cause applies. Misalignment is the other documented possibility for this temperature symptom.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Verify the asset serial before ordering or fitting parts. Kit one HF3-450B pre-set cartridge mechanical seal and one new HF3-120 casing gasket. Do not fit HF3-450 on this serial. HF3-450B requires no sleeve measurement for seal setting.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before opening it. Apply the site controls for residual sodium-hypochlorite-dosed water; the supplied evidence confirms dosing but does not provide the site PPE or decontamination procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly using suitable lifting equipment: its documented mass is 68 kg and lifting equipment is required. The back pull-out design permits removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the sleeve for scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. The cartridge's pre-set design eliminates sleeve measurement for seal setting, but does not eliminate this scoring inspection. Inspect the removed seal faces and look for evidence of dry running.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Because the drive-end housing was 71 °C, check grease quantity and bearing condition. If wear, noise or a high-temperature bearing condition is confirmed, replace the drive-end and non-drive-end bearings as a pair rather than replacing only one bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new HF3-450B cartridge seal and a new HF3-120 casing gasket; fit a new HF3-455 sleeve if the scoring criterion requires it. The casing gasket is to be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten the fasteners. Table 5 values for lightly oiled threads are: M24 impeller nut 160 Nm, M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm where disturbed. For the HF3-450B seal gland nuts, use 30 Nm under SB-2026-014, not the manual's superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment. Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and correct any condition that could allow dry running. On return to service, document seal leakage, housing-surface temperature and vibration velocity on both bearing housings; classify the highest vibration reading with Figure 3. Weekly vibration measurement on both housings is required thereafter. Record any continuing leakage for further assessment because no numerical leak acceptance criterion is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; required replacement for HF3-450 on this serial. Do not substitute HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new with the seal and replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, conditional: inspect during disassembly and supply/fit one only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth; current evidence does not establish that replacement is required.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3, conditional: required only if bearing inspection establishes the replacement condition; if replaced, it must be replaced together with HF3-510.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3, conditional: required together with HF3-512 when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before seal replacement or removal of the back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use suitable lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; manual lifting without equipment is not permitted by the documented instruction.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Treat the pump and drained/residual water as sodium-hypochlorite-dosed. Obtain the site's chemical-exposure, PPE and decontamination requirements before opening the pump; those specific requirements are not included in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge and must be addressed before return to service.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any subsequent running checks, Figure 3 requires the pump to be stopped if vibration enters Zone D, 7.1 to 11.0 mm/s RMS, where damage is likely. The bearing-housing temperature alarm and trip remain 80 °C and 90 °C respectively.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, using the standard labour allowance.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours with 1 technician. Plan this allowance because shaft-seal leakage requires an alignment check and laser alignment is mandatory after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing-pair replacement: add 6.0 hours with 2 technicians only if inspection establishes that bearing replacement is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection: the Revision D manual parts list identifies HF3-450, a component-type mechanical seal. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, explicitly applies to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above, says not to fit HF3-450, and requires pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B. P-105 is exactly HF3-22000 and therefore falls inside, not below, the bulletin range. Use HF3-450B for this asset; the manual choice remains applicable only to pumps below that serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, while the serial-applicable service bulletin specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B and identifies 25 Nm as the former value. Use 30 Nm for this repair. The bulletin does not supersede the other documented Table 5 torques.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve instructions are complementary rather than a reason to omit inspection: the manual requires inspection for scoring, while the bulletin says the pre-set HF3-450B needs no sleeve measurement for seal setting and separately requires sleeve replacement when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Accordingly, omit sleeve measurement for cartridge setting but retain the scoring inspection and 0.1 mm replacement criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Confirm that the reported 3.9 mm/s vibration is RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, identify the measurement location, and provide the other bearing-housing reading so that the highest reading can be classified as required (C06, C07).",
    "Which seal is currently installed, and whether inspection finds worn/cracked faces, dry-run damage or misalignment, is not stated in the report. The asset-specific HF3-450 early-failure mechanism therefore remains conditional on the installed seal type (C09, C13).",
    "The shaft-sleeve scoring depth is unknown, so the conditional HF3-455 replacement cannot be confirmed until disassembly and inspection (C10, C13).",
    "Bearing grease quantity, noise, wear and internal condition are unknown. Confirm these before releasing the conditional bearing pair and associated labour (C09, C10).",
    "The evidence does not provide sodium-hypochlorite concentration, site PPE, decontamination, flushing or residual-chemical handling instructions; obtain the applicable site procedure before opening the pump (C16).",
    "No quantitative allowable shaft-seal leakage rate or post-repair leak acceptance criterion is supplied; obtain the applicable acceptance criterion if visual observation and documented troubleshooting instructions are insufficient for close-out (C09, C10)."
  ]
}
